From 4ccd1e3784264e07fcbe169c1bd28e360aabe279 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: issakakar <Issakakar@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:20:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] perf(editor): keep the viewport cull on the Set path, and
 trim dead engine API

The cull is the one consumer that probes every shape on the page for a result
of a few hundred, so the cost is all lookups and a small Set is a smaller table
to hit repeatedly than a page-sized id-to-slot map. The index-level benchmark
puts the query path 10-30% behind there; in the editor the two are within the
noise floor. Set wins on the measurement that can tell them apart, so the cull
goes back to getShapeIdsInsideBounds and the query path is left to the
consumers whose probes are proportional to what the search matched.

Also drops readBBox, searchAll and the maxEntries/minEntries fields from
FlatRTree: nothing calls them, and the fields read as if M were configurable
when every stride below is a source literal.
